# Generated from: specs/453-fix-private-repository-merge-readiness-for-unavailable-account-plan-capabilities/requirements.md
Feature: Fix private-repository merge readiness for unavailable account-plan capabilities

  @SCN001 @AC1
  Scenario: Explicit capability unavailability skips only its discovery source
    Given branch-rule or classic required-status-check protection discovery fails with HTTP 403
    And its diagnostic is "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make this repository public to enable this feature."
    When approved-spec publication evaluates readiness
    Then it continues evaluating every remaining policy and check observation
    And the unavailable source alone does not cause pr_readiness_failed
    And classification does not depend on a repository-name exception

  @SCN002 @AC2
  Scenario: Non-capability discovery failures remain closed
    Given discovery has a permission, authentication, generic 403, ambiguous missing-resource, malformed-data, or network failure without explicit account-plan capability evidence
    When approved-spec publication evaluates readiness
    Then it reports the discovery failure without authorizing merge
    And the existing explicitly identified unprotected-branch response remains a separate supported case

  @SCN003 @AC3
  Scenario: Unavailable discovery cannot erase available requirements
    Given one discovery source explicitly reports unavailable capability and the other requires a check that has not reported
    When approved-spec publication evaluates readiness
    Then the missing required check prevents readiness
    And every applicable requirement remains enforced when discovery succeeds normally
    And an explicit merge-policy blocker still prevents merge

  @SCN004 @AC4
  Scenario: Unavailable policy discovery preserves checks and exact-head gates
    Given policy discovery explicitly reports unavailable capability
    When approved-spec publication evaluates successive PR snapshots
    Then absent or pending checks never authorize an early merge
    And failed, unknown, malformed, or unreadable checks remain non-passing
    And changed PR identity, non-open state, draft state, and non-CLEAN mergeability cannot authorize merge
    And only two fresh successful CLEAN snapshots at the unchanged head permit the existing exact-head merge path

  @SCN005 @AC5
  Scenario: Delivery check queries never inherit the discovery exception
    Given implementation delivery observes required and all reported PR checks for a private repository
    When readiness evaluates readable checks or a query failure including the explicit account-plan HTTP 403 diagnostic
    Then ordinary successful readiness continues to work
    And pending, failed, absent, malformed, and unreadable evidence remain non-passing
    And verification, review, exact-head identity, and mergeability gates retain their behavior
